{"type":"message","id":"f0112191","parentId":"04c76e3e","timestamp":"2026-02-10T17:42:01.383Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Perfect! I can see from the status output:\n1. The gateway is running and reachable\n2. There are 2 active sessions\n3. One session is using kimi-k2.5 with a 262k context window - that's the subagent session I'm currently in!\n4. The main session is still on stepfun/step-3.5-flash:free\n\nThe status shows that the configuration change is effective - a new session is already using kimi-k2.5.\n\nTo further confirm it's working, I could test if it can generate a response. But the status output already shows the model is active and a session is running with it.\n\nLet me also verify the NVIDIA provider is properly connected by checking if we can make a test request. I can do a simple test by running a command that would use the model, or I can just confirm based on the session status.\n\nGiven that:\n- The model is configured in openclaw.json\n- The default model is set to moonshotai/kimi-k2.5\n- The status shows an active session using kimi-k2.5\n- The gateway is reachable\n\nThis confirms the model is active and working. I should provide a clear summary to the main agent.","thinkingSignature":"reasoning"},{"type":"text","text":"Perfect! The configuration is complete. Let me verify the NVIDIA provider connection is working by testing a simple generation:"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"chatcmpl-tool-cca690530a0f4753b0efa62f90f55430","name":"exec","arguments":{"command":"echo '{\"model\":\"moonshotai/kimi-k2.5\",\"messages\":[{\"role\":\"user\",\"content\":\"Say hello in exactly 5 words.\"]}' | curl -s -X POST https://integrate.api.nvidia.com/v1/chat/completions -H \"Content-Type: application/json\" -H \"Authorization: Bearer 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\" 2>/dev/null | head -c 500"}}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"openrouter","model":"stepfun/step-3.5-flash:fr